## Why This Is Asked

Tests a practical cross‑account data flow with strict data isolation, field‑level masking, and robust rollback handling in a beginner‑to‑intermediate context.

## Key Concepts

- Cross‑account IAM roles and trust policies
- KMS data‑key management (per‑tenant keys)
- ETL processing (Lambda or Glue)
- Data masking, validation, and rollback procedures

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: redacting sensitive fields
function maskPII(record){
  if(record.hasOwnProperty('name')) record.name = 'REDACTED';
  if(record.hasOwnProperty('email')) record.email = 'REDACTED';
  return record;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would schema evolution be handled without leaking PII?
- How would you monitor and alert if an unmasked field slips through the ETL?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests cross-account log delivery, least privilege, and lifecycle handling in a real SaaS pattern.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-account IAM roles and bucket policies
- TLS-only S3 access and private endpoints
- CMK encryption and CloudTrail validation
- Onboarding/offboarding automation and rollback

## Code Example
```json
// Central bucket policy sketch
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::<central-id>:role/TenantLogPublisher"},
      "Action": "s3:PutObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::central-logs-bucket/tenant-prefix/*",
      "Condition": {
        "Bool": {"aws:SecureTransport": "true"}
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
// Trust policy sketch for TenantLogPublisher (in central/account_root)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"Service": "delivery.logs.amazonaws.com"},
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:SourceAccount": "<central-id>"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test end-to-end log delivery across accounts?
- How would you handle rotation of the CMK and rotation of the tenant role?
